It's a series of six books from Michael Moorcock called

  1. Elric from Melnibone
  2. The Sailor on the Seas of Fate
  3. The Weird of the White Wolf
  4. The Vanishing Tower
  5. The Bane of the Black Sword
  6. Stormbringer

I have read a German edition of these collected in one book, a total of
1000 pages.

As Fitzdraco wrote, Elric is an anti hero and the story is very gloomy.
It is different to most other fantasy I've read; it's very fascinating!
IMO, it is worth to read the book(s). (You may start with one and then
decide to continue or not.)

BTW, I, in no way, consider the books spoilerish.

